-- gap[104] · a constant condition INSIDE a constant condition.
--
-- Two tail slots stacked: `print("innerlast")` is the inner block's tail and
-- `print("outerlast")` is the outer block's, so a repair that lowers one level
-- of tail expression and not the recursive case loses `outerlast` only. That is
-- a one-line difference in the expected value and it is the reason this row
-- prints four distinguishable strings instead of one.

main = (): i64
    if 42 > 10
        if 7 > 3
            print("inner")
            print("innerlast")
        print("outerlast")
    print("after")
    0
